out.push(h2('16.7  Review & Mediate: a judge, the judged, and a reader who shares neither field'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready – Unit 16 quiz'));
out.push(A('**1** _…on the ground **that** criterion 3 was decided…_ ⚠ **Delete _of_.**   **2** _…because the word **was said** once._   **3** _…what a proposal can always **produce**._ ⚠ **Delete _it_.**   **4** _…falls **outside** what I am able to assess._ ⚠ **Delete _of_.**   **5** _**Had** I known the figure…_   **6** _…record that they **could not** assess it._ ⚠ **Delete _to_.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**b** ⚠ **That the appeal was unnecessary.** **Mr Sabbagh used the ground Mr Tayara printed, in the words Mr Tayara printed it in** — **and a reply that calls it unnecessary has punished a man for taking the route the judge laid out for him, and has taught everybody who hears of it that a printed ground is a trap.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the fourth mediation of Book 2 and the sixteenth of the level, and what is new is that there are four accounts, all accurate, and the one that settles the matter has not been seen by any of the three parties.** **Do not let the room look for a villain.** **The judge declared his limit; the judged used it; the adviser answered the question he was asked.** **A clerk sent a file and did not send a line, and a fortnight was spent on a document asking for something that had already been given** — **and that is the cheapest failure in the unit and the commonest in any organisation this room works in.** ⚠ **The finding of the cycle is the count on item 2.** **A judge from outside the subject produced a figure he said he could not interpret, and the specialist says that figure is the finding of the lesson.** **Neither could have produced it alone.** **Say that at the end and not before** — **because it is the case for the whole unit and the room will hear it as a consolation if it arrives early.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Pair A, the appraisal and the adviser)'));
