out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report – mediation (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Khoury said the inspector gets the letter and it is three lines, because the appeal is against a document the inspector holds, the remedy is already in train, and the only person who can tell Mr Sabbagh that is the office that sent item 6 away on the twelfth. Mr Tayara said what must not be said is that the appeal was unnecessary, and that is exactly it and it is the most tempting sentence in the cycle, because he used the ground that Mr Tayara printed, in the words Mr Tayara printed it in, and a reply that calls it unnecessary has punished a man for taking the route the judge laid out for him. Mrs Oueidat said right about the ground and wrong about the remedy, and Mr Zahreddine said those are two answers and the appeal gets both: item 6 was assessed by somebody who recorded that he could not, granted and already acted on, and setting the whole appraisal aside, refused, because the other five items were assessed by a competent judge and nobody has said otherwise. Dr Qabbani said he spent a fortnight on it, and a fortnight on a document asking for a thing he had been given six days before he started, and the fault there is not his and not Mr Tayara\'s: the office acted and told nobody. Mrs Rizk asked whether the adviser\'s note should go to him, and it should, and the note says the demonstration showed what he said it showed, so item 6 is in his favour, and it also says the finding of the lesson is in item 2, which nobody has mentioned and which is not in his favour at all. Mr Attar said so the good news and the bad news are in one document, and Mr Tayara said it is the item he counted: nine of forty-one questions to four pupils in the front row, and he wrote that he was reporting what he counted and not what he judged, and the adviser, who can judge it, says that is the finding of the lesson. Mrs Khoury said that is the unit arriving at its own point from the opposite end, because the judge outside the field supplied a count he could not interpret and the specialist interpreted it, and neither could have produced the finding alone. Mrs Tarabishi asked whether Mr Tayara comes out of this well, and he comes out as the man who wrote the ground of the appeal against himself and then turned out to have supplied the finding, and both came from the same habit. Mrs Ajouz asked whether anybody is at fault, and the office, for acting and not writing, and nobody else. Mr Shihabi asked about the three lines, and the ground is granted and already acted on, the remedy is refused and here is why, and the adviser\'s note goes to Mr Sabbagh entire. And Mr Tayara said the thing he will take away is that he quoted him: the sentence in which he said he could not do his job is now the first line of a document asking for his appraisal to be set aside, and he would write it again tomorrow.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **Three lines to carry out of the unit, in this order, and the order is the teaching.** **First Mr Tayara\'s count: nine of forty-one questions to four pupils in the front row, reported as a count and not a judgement.** **Then the adviser\'s note: that count is the finding of the lesson.** **Then Mrs Khoury\'s sentence: the judge outside the field supplied a count he could not interpret, the specialist interpreted it, and neither could have produced the finding alone.** **That is what a declared limit is for, and it is a larger claim than modesty.**'));
out.push(S('Board clinic – typical mistakes'));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ _This appeal was unnecessary_ → **the man used the ground you printed.**   **2** **One answer for two questions** → **the party appeals again on the half you did not address.**   **3** ⚠ **The adviser\'s note summarised** → **it arrives as the good half.**   **4** **A letter to the judged instead of the office** → **the office holds the document and made the error.**   **5** ⚠ **A culprit found among the three parties** → **the office acted and did not write; that is the whole fault.**   **6** **A concession withdrawn in the next clause** → **16.4\'s _although_, arriving in a reply.**'));
out.push(S('Board – the four accounts, and what each one can and cannot see'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Run this at 16.7 Stage 2a with the four accounts on the board and the last column empty.** **The room fills it.** **The point is not that somebody is wrong: all four are accurate, and the value of the exercise is in the last column, where every party is blind to something that one of the others can see.**'));
